01</year><volume>41</volume><issue>5</issue><fpage>1211</fpage><lpage>1222</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11555299</pub-id></element-citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-group><fig id="fig1" position="float"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>The construction of pMD-<italic>asd</italic>p1234 (<italic>Cm</italic>). </p></caption><graphic xlink:href="JBB2009-646380.001"/></fig><fig id="fig2" position="float"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>The screening strategy for the  <italic>SP</italic>  &#x00394;<italic>asd</italic> mutant.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="JBB2009-646380.002"/></fig><fig id="fig3" position="float"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>Genetic organization of a recombinant construct containing a defined deletion. The map shows the recombinant &#x00394;<italic>asd</italic> (1488 bp) region deleted from the  <italic>SP</italic> genome. The open arrow indicates the coding region of the <italic>asd</italic>  gene (<italic>Cm</italic><sup>R</sup> gene), and dotted lines represent the limits of the deleted region. The deletion is shown as an open triangle, and the sizes of the flanking regions adjacent to the deletion on the suicide vector are indicated. The position and orientation of PCR primers used in this study are indicated by filled arrows on the map of the wt DNA. The sizes of the PCR amplified products from the wt, the  <italic>SP</italic>  &#x00394;<italic>asd</italic>   (<italic>Cm</italic>)   mutant, and the  <italic>SP</italic>  &#x00394;<italic>asd</italic> mutant are 1796 bp, 1360 bp, and 328 bp, respectively.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="JBB2009-646380.003"/></fig><fig id="fig4" position="float"><label>Figure 4</label><caption><p>The growth curves of the &#x00394;<italic>asd</italic> mutant, the &#x00394;<italic>asd</italic> mutant   (<italic>Cm</italic>)   and the parental strain S06004 in LB media with DAP.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="JBB2009-646380.004"/></fig><fig id="fig5" position="float"><label>Figure 5</label><caption><p>PCR identification of the  <italic>SP</italic>  &#x00394;<italic>asd</italic>   (<italic>Cm</italic>)   mutants.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="JBB2009-646380.005"/></fig><fig id="fig6" position="float"><label>Figure 6</label><caption><p>dsRED expression in the  <italic>SP</italic>  &#x00394;<italic>asd</italic> mutant (pYA3334-dsRED).     <italic>SP</italic>  &#x00394;<italic>asd</italic> mutant (pYA3334-dsRED) colonies showed red fluorescence on LB plates without DAP.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="JBB2009-646380.006"/></fig><fig id="fig7" position="float"><label>Figure 7</label><caption><p>FACS analysis of dsRED expression in the different passages of the  <italic>SP</italic>  &#x00394;<italic>asd</italic> mutant (pYA3334-dsRED). S2-control: control for the  <italic>SP</italic>  &#x00394;<italic>asd</italic> mutant (pYA3334); S2-2: The 2nd passage of the  <italic>SP</italic>  &#x00394;<italic>asd</italic> mutant (pYA3334-dsRED);  S2-20: The 20th passage of the  <italic>SP</italic>  &#x00394;<italic>asd</italic> mutant (pYA3334-dsRED).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="JBB2009-646380.007"/></fig><table-wrap id="tab1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Strains and plasmids used in this study.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Name</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">  Description</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"> Source</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"> Reference</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="6" colspan="1">Strains </td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>S. Pullorum</italic> S06004 (<italic>Nal</italic><sup>R</sup>)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Recipient</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Lab collection </td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>&#x00